      "id": "K2",
      "title": "A death, then a curse（死、そして呪い）",
      "text": "When Lord Carnarvon died in Cairo in April 1923, newspapers around the world linked his death to Tutankhamun's tomb. They quoted Arthur Conan Doyle on a spirit-like force guarding it. On the same pages, other experts disagreed. The curse story grew from pages like these.",
